A||||7||enslaved||tranny mounts||||1||
Z||000000||enslaved||08-21-2001||12:55 PM||||I have a bad vibration when i go about 5-10-15 mph. it stops when i go any faster. I noticed the tranny mounts are broke... can you guys suggest the easiest way to replace them? also... the engine rocks forward about 1-2 inches when i accelerate... would replacing the dogbone fix this? I dont have the money nor the resourses for new engine mounts...<P>(btw its a 84 se)<p>[This message has been edited by enslaved (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-21-2001||01:04 PM||||new mounts from NAPA are under $70 for all of them. <A HREF="http://www.napaonline.com" TARGET=_blank>www.napaonline.com</A>  check em out. <P>you can get them one at a time but don't install them one at a time.. they all need to be replaced at the same time or you'll just destroy the new ones with the old worn out crappy ones. the untimate dog bone isn't a must but for more spirited driving it does help.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">         <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
Z||000002||enslaved||08-21-2001||01:07 PM||||heh, thanks..<P>If i do buy these... What will i need to put those bad boys in? i sure as heck dont have a lift. I have a couple jacks and jack stands. lol. do i have to lift the engine? I dont have a way to lift the engine. And auto shops want like 800 bux in labor to do it!!!! I sure as hell wont pay 800 bux if i can do it myself. thats for damn sure. Any ideas? thanks for your help||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||08-21-2001||01:26 PM||||You can do all of them with a jack and a 15mm cup. You don't need an engine lift. You can lift the engine from the bottom just enough to pull out/in the mounts. Just check the front engine mount well before replacing. Mine with 160K miles of beating was ok and it was hell to get to those screws (88 Formula). Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||08-21-2001||10:08 PM||||I changed all of mine.  The Sealed Power mounts from Discount Auto were misaligned (the studs), so I got the brand Autozone carries.  Fit perfectly,and it was under $30 for all three mounts.  I had to unbolt the dogbone to lift the engine enough to fit in the mount behind the balancer.  Use a block of wood between your jack and the oil pan, or you'll dimple it.  The transaxle mounts are even easier, since they are two pieces (the bracket and the rubberized mount itself).  I seem to remember the exhaust pipe getting in the way, though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||enslaved||08-22-2001||12:03 AM||||Well, if i dont get around to the mounts.. would a nice dogbone hold my engine still for a while? i just dont want the rocking to break my exhaust!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Cuz i mean... it rocks like 3 freakin inches! any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000006||enslaved||08-22-2001||12:32 AM||||I gotta know some opinions! I am buying parts for my car tommorow morning.. and i gotta know if i should buy a dogbone!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||08-22-2001||12:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by enslaved:<BR><B>I gotta know some opinions! I am buying parts for my car tommorow morning.. and i gotta know if i should buy a dogbone!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If the holes in thr rubber is stretched-yes, otherwise get the trans mounts for now.  I saw someone's pics on the forum...stretched like an inch!  Not good!<P>I converted my trans mounts to polyurethane.<P>Joe<BR>||||reg||1
